WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.984
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.325
JIA LI: Hi, everyone.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.120
I'm Jia.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.590
Here today, I'm talking
about how, at Cloud AI,

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.750
we're inspired by
customer needs.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:28.310
AI has the potential to
change every industry,

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:33.250
from transportation to health
care, from retail to education.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:44.700
However, there is a big gap
between what's possible with AI

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.610
and what's within reach
for our customers.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:58.455
This gap reveals a lack of
awareness on both sides.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.940
On one side, many
traditional companies

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.780
lack an understanding of
AI, which makes it hard

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.930
for them to benefit from it.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:22.750
Machine learning development
is an extremely complex cycle.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:29.050
From collecting data, designing
model, tuning model parameters,

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:35.260
updating the model, evaluating
it, and iterate the process,

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:39.430
every single step would require
machine learning expertise.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.450
Unfortunately, of the world's
21 million developers,

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:52.590
only one million or so have
data science background.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.790
And thousands of them have
deep learning or machine

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:56.790
learning expertise.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:04.160
And on the other
side, technologists

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.220
who are driving the
development of AI

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:12.050
lack an understanding about
traditional industries.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:17.110
As a result, many problems
that could benefit from AI

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:21.072
remains unsolved.

00:02:21.072 --> 00:02:26.630
At Google Cloud, we're trying to
bring our customers and the AI

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:31.920
experts together on
the shared platform.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.200
We try to help our customers
to understand AI and make

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.180
its capability more accessible.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.420
Through this
process, we developed

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:47.260
the first-hand understanding
of their world,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:50.350
the challenges they are facing.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:56.320
And by combining this with
the AI expertise at Google,

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.305
we can address their problems
in powerful new ways.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.670
By understanding
the diverse range

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:09.080
of needs in today's
enterprise environment,

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.740
we're delivering the
power of AI in the form

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:17.630
that we hope to meet our
customers where they are.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:25.140
We provide AI technology across
a wide spectrum of solutions.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.950
On one side, for the
most advanced machine

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.490
learning experts, we provide
the most powerful machine

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:36.200
learning tools for them
to build their vision,

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:45.990
like TPUs, TensorFlow, Kubeflow,
Cloud ML Engine, et cetera.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:51.400
On the other are the customers
who understand the value of AI,

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:56.670
but don't have the
expertise to put it in use.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:03.240
For them, we offer simple tools
that deliver immediate results,

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.480
like the Machine Learning APIs.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:13.240
And in between, we offer a
growing range of solutions

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:19.269
that blend the ease of use and
sophisticated capabilities,

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:22.489
such as Contact Center
we announced yesterday.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.540
Furthermore, we believe in
delivering maximum results

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.950
for every customer,
regardless of their expertise.

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:39.350
Consider Cloud TPU,
for example, the custom

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:44.390
chips that dramatically
accelerate machine learning

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:46.460
tasks.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:50.720
With minimal amount
of code, advanced user

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.100
can run their TensorFlow
models on TPUs

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.710
and experience an
immediate boost.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:05.010
But even novices can rely
on the performance boost

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:12.530
from the latest Google hardware,
as APIs like Translation API

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:17.190
can automatically leverage
TPUs behind the scenes.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.880
No matter what's
your level of scale,

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.870
we want to ensure you
benefit from our most

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.370
powerful technology.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:34.070
We call this democratizing
AI, but there's

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:40.540
much more we can do to
make AI more accessible.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:44.780
To explain where our
technology is going next,

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:48.640
I'd like to share a
bit of the history

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.420
that I've witnessed in my own
career in computer vision.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:59.010
Image classification is
among the greatest success

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.550
stories in our field.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.780
In recent years, it has
been going through a lot

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.770
of significant improvement.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.650
And now, we're thinking
about how do we

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:21.200
expand the success of image
recognition to other areas?

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:29.050
But we are facing a lot
of challenges in doing so.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:32.590
The first challenge is data.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:37.600
Years were spent collecting
millions of images

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:42.560
to train algorithms to
understand what they see.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:45.770
The second is
algorithm development.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:49.880
It took hundreds of
researchers decades

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.960
to refine the algorithm
behind this single goal.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:07:00.260
A big part of democratizing
AI will be finding better ways

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:04.615
to replicate what has made image
recognition such a success.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:10.980
This is the promise of AutoML.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:16.110
AutoML makes it possible to
customize our most advanced

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:20.190
machine learning models to your
customized and specific use

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:25.290
case, all without writing
any machine learning code.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.410
Our first release
came earlier this year

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.890
in the form of Cloud
AutoML Vision, which

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:40.330
makes it possible to train the
Cloud Vision API to recognize

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:44.080
entirely new image categories.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:48.640
Keller Williams Realty
is using AutoML Vision

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:52.430
to bring to market the
most advanced home search

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:56.230
experience for consumers.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:59.860
By training a custom
model to recognize

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:04.360
common elements of
furnishing and architecture,

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.950
customers can automatically
search home listing photos

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:14.230
to find their specific preferred
features, like granite counter

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:17.530
tops, or even more general
style, like modern.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:25.420
And here at Next, we
have introduced two

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:28.300
additional AutoML features--

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.830
AutoML Natural Language
and AutoML Translation.

00:08:34.419 --> 00:08:38.080
With AutoML natural
language, customers

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:42.100
can train custom models
to accurately recognize

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.220
domain-specific
content in their text.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:56.450
For example, in one of our
customer, Hearst Newspapers,

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:59.970
they're one of the
world's largest publishers

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:02.910
of magazines and newspapers.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.700
They have been always
looking for better ways

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.335
to manage their content.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:15.150
At Hearst Newspaper,
they are looking forward

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:20.550
to leverage Cloud ML,
AutoML Natural Language

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:26.710
to customize domain-specific
text models for their newspaper

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.800
accountant.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:34.200
And that has been providing
high accuracy for their needs,

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.460
without writing any
machine learning code.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.260
AutoML Translation helps to
recognize jargon and terms

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:48.050
specific to your domain.

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:52.910
And the result is
actually to translation

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:56.150
to capture the
context and nuance

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.340
that your customer will expect.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:05.440
So customers all
over the world have

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:11.320
been finding ways to improve
translation with AutoML.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:16.480
For example, Nikkei, a media
company based in Japan,

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:21.400
is evaluating AutoML for
translating international news

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.470
articles.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:28.720
By leveraging AutoML, it
meets the customization

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:30.430
needs from them.

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:33.410
And they have been very
impressed by the accuracy.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.850
AI is still a very
nascent space.

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:45.200
And we know that each of you
face some unique challenge.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.780
We are eager to learn
them and help solve them.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:55.980
That will require us to keep
a close conversation with you.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.270
Let's talk about the
problems in your industry

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:03.150
and what are the ideal
outcome look like.

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:08.210
And let's work together to
use the latest AI technology

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:11.550
to make that vision a reality.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:13.790
Thank you.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:17.780
Now, I'd like to welcome
Stefan to the stage

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:21.660
to share how we are
partnering with SAP to bring

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:28.210
AI and enterprise software to
the physical world using Google

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:28.710
Cloud.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:29.210
Thank you.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.690
STEFAN NUSSER: Thanks, Jia.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.670
[APPLAUSE]

00:11:36.129 --> 00:11:37.170
Good afternoon, everyone.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.890
My name is Stephan Nusser,
I'm product manager

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:42.260
for Cloud AI in Europe.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.990
Here at Google Cloud, one
of our primary objectives

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:48.500
is democratizing AI, lowering
the barriers to entry

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.720
and making it as easy as
possible for customers

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:55.080
all over the world to put its
remarkable capabilities to use.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:58.250
As AI becomes more
accessible, other technologies

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.990
benefit as well.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:03.510
We see an opportunity here to
use the combined power of AI

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:07.640
and the Cloud to make automation
more accessible to industry

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.530
and to businesses of all sizes.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:14.516
To understand how, let's
take a look at [NON-ENGLISH],,

00:12:14.516 --> 00:12:17.420
Industry 4.0, and the
state of automation today.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.010
There's an exciting
transformation

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.200
on the way in the
industrial sector.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:28.340
Manufacturing operations
and the entire supply chain

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:29.900
are being digitized.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:34.845
This is known as Industry 4.0.

00:12:34.845 --> 00:12:38.230
It involves sensorizing machines
and also the environment.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:40.450
Industrial sector
companies want to use

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:45.190
that sensor data to drive
machine learning and AI.

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:48.070
This promises to enable
new levels of optimization

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:49.000
and learning.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.640
The ultimate goal is to make
processes that are currently

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:57.460
manually operated be controlled
much more efficiently.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:00.440
Automation plays an important
part in this process.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.370
Now historically, automation
has been highly customized

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.200
in silos with high
upfront costs.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:09.010
And as a result of
that, vendor lock-in.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.780
It's also inflexible.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.670
If you can afford
automation, you'll

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:15.890
structure your entire
environment around it.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:19.060
Today, we're seeing exciting
trends in automation.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.160
Collaborative
robots, like the ones

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.041
shown on this slide
that are equipped

00:13:23.041 --> 00:13:25.540
with modern sensors and open
software layers that are easier

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.090
to program, these
collaborative robots

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:30.760
promise to transform how we
do automation, especially

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:33.460
in less-structured environment
where these robots can

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.765
work side-by-side with humans.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.246
So how do we digitize
the physical world

00:13:40.246 --> 00:13:42.370
in less-structured
environments, like the warehouse

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.110
that you see on this slide?

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:46.870
It's easy to capture sensor
readings from big machines,

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:48.750
but it's much harder
to digitize goods

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:52.150
in storage or containers of
goods, like bins, or pallets,

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:55.360
or shelves, or boxes,
especially if human workers are

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.740
in the same workspace and
manually move these goods

00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:59.530
and containers around?

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:01.630
We believe we can solve
some of these challenges

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:03.490
with the help of
collaborative robots

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:06.550
and by harnessing the
power of AI and the Cloud.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:09.440
And we're not the only ones
who see this opportunity.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:13.380
Let me tell you a little
about our partner, SAP.

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:16.120
SAP is the world leader in
enterprise applications.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.850
They manage business processes
of large and medium-sized

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.160
companies across the world.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.080
Think orders, parts,
or inventory levels.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:28.240
Their roots are in Europe
and in the industrial sector.

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:30.010
SAP is working with
their customers

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:32.790
to gradually transition
workloads from on-premise

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:33.850
to the Cloud.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.910
That, combined with their
deep industry expertise,

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:40.690
makes them a unique
and strong GCP partner.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.760
Industry 4.0 is a huge
opportunity for SAP

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:46.060
to optimize not only
business processes,

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:49.410
but to take this optimization
closer to the physical world,

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:52.910
based on, for example, real
time awareness of good, pallets,

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.830
or trolleys in a warehouse.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.460
Shorter feedback loops
combined with readily available

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.580
automation will translate
into increased efficiency

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.760
and agility for SAP's customers.

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:06.580
To capture this opportunity,
SAP is looking for ways

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.460
to manage and orchestrate
collaborative robots

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:11.560
from different
vendors and to tap

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:16.730
into insights about the physical
world for better optimization.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:19.820
The Cloud AI engineering
team in Munich, in Germany,

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:21.650
is working on an
open Cloud Robotics

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.840
platform that adds
critical infrastructure

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.880
for collaborative robots.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:28.340
It builds on mature
GCP technologies

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.410
and provides
foundational capabilities

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:34.010
for Cloud-enabled
automation solutions.

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.980
Our Cloud Robotics
platform securely

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:38.500
connects robots with the Cloud.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.420
It enables distribution
of software

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:42.550
and other digital
assets to the robots,

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:45.310
using Kubernetes containers.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:48.130
It provides infrastructure
for collecting log data,

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:50.650
for uploading it, monitoring
it, and creating dashboards

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.750
using Stackdriver.

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.390
It also provides infrastructure
for sensor data collection,

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.370
aggregation, transfer
to the Cloud,

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.980
and processing without data
management biplanes, Bigtable,

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:03.760
BigQuery, Dataflow, and more.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.760
Our objective here is to solve
these common infrastructure

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.920
problems for the
entire industry.

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:11.560
Our Cloud Robotics platform
will be open source

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:13.720
and will be built on open APIs.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:16.140
We'll also provide the
interfaces needed for customers

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.380
to port their data
to other platforms.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:20.650
So there's no window locking.

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.150
This Cloud Robotics
platform will

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:25.780
be available to early adopters
at the beginning of next year.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:27.820
On top of this
infrastructure, we

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:31.300
will offer Cloud services
that leverage our AI platform

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.370
and solve several
critical customer pain

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:35.540
points for the mission
with collaborative robots.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:40.560
Our SLAM service uses
data from sensors,

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.600
like lighters or depth cameras.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.490
It allows robots
to create a map,

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:46.740
localize themselves
relative to that map,

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.450
and recognize static landmarks.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:57.080
We further analyze that sensor
data to discover walls, doors,

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:00.830
shelves, tables, chairs,
and other essential elements

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.030
of the robot's workspace.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:09.060
Using that same data, we can
also discover known objects

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.744
in their pose in the workspace.

00:17:11.744 --> 00:17:13.619
This would allow the
robot to detect and plan

00:17:13.619 --> 00:17:14.819
operations on these items.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:21.829
Where are we going with this?

00:17:21.829 --> 00:17:23.540
There is a broader vision here.

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:26.780
Our infrastructure enables
reusable assets on the robot

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.560
and in the cloud.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.310
It can support not only the
services I just described,

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:35.390
but also serve as a foundation
for third-party software.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:37.490
Our plan is to work
with our partners

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.380
to grow this platform
into an ecosystem,

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:42.940
using an app store for
easy software distribution.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:46.100
SAP as a developer,
and their customers,

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.770
benefit from easier
creation and deployment

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:51.270
